//            free-run) ─► timebase sweep with a vertical delay line
//         ─► beam path (dwell-weighted energy) ─► phosphor (GPU)
//
// Phosphor: two-component persistence (fast + slow channels, each saturating),
// exact moving-Gaussian deposit per path segment, so fast edges are dim and
// slow parts glow — like a real beam. Halation in the faceplate is blurred
// emission, confined to the screen.
// ============================================================================
